To model the mission description into a goal model for multi-robot systems, we decompose the mission into hierarchical goals and tasks, considering parallel and sequential execution, fallback cases, and task assignments.

### Goal Model

| Goal ID | Goal Title                  | Text                                                                                   | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type       | Relation |
|--------|----------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------|----------------|----------|
| G1     | Deliver Required Resources  | Ensure resources are collected and delivered to the specified location.             | -                 | Achieve Goal   | -        |
| G2     | Collect Resources           | Gather required resources from storage locations.                                  | ;                 | Perform Goal   | G1       |
| G3     | Deliver Resources           | Transport collected resources to the specified location.                            | ;                 | Perform Goal   | G1       |
| G4     | Navigate to Storage         | Move to the storage location to collect resources.                                 | -                 | Perform Goal   | G2       |
| G5     | Request Resources           | Communicate with storage to retrieve specific resources.                           | -                 | Perform Goal   | G2       |
| G6     | Wait for Retrieval          | Wait until resources are retrieved from storage.                                    | -                 | Perform Goal   | G2       |
| G7     | Handle Low Battery (Collect)| If battery drops to 10%, recharge and assign mission to another robot.             | -                 | Perform Goal   | G2       |
| G8     | Navigate to Delivery Location| Move to the delivery location to drop off resources.                              | -                 | Perform Goal   | G3       |
| G9     | Transport Resources         | Carry resources from storage to delivery location.                                | -                 | Perform Goal   | G3       |
| G10    | Handle Low Battery (Delivery)| If battery drops to 30%, return resources to checkpoint and assign to another robot.| -                 | Perform Goal   | G3       |
| G11    | Ensure Resource Delivery    | Confirm resources are delivered to the correct location.                           | -                 | Achieve Goal   | G3       |
| G12    | Trigger Alert               | Send alert if resource return to checkpoint fails.                                | -                 | Perform Goal   | G10      |

### Task Model

| Task ID | Task Title                     | Text                                                                                   | Relation | Location                  | Number of Robots |
|---------|--------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|---------------------------|------------------|
| AT1     | Navigate to Storage            | Move to the designated storage area.                                               | AND      | Storage Location          | 1                |
| AT2     | Request Resources              | Send request for specific resources.                                                 | AND      | Storage Location          | 1                |
| AT3     | Wait for Retrieval             | Stay at storage until resources are retrieved.                                    | AND      | Storage Location          | 1                |
| AT4     | Recharge Station              | Return to recharging station when battery is low.                                | AND      | Recharging Station        | 1                |
| AT5     | Assign Mission                 | Transfer mission to another robot.                                                 | AND      | Recharging Station        | [1, n]           |
| AT6     | Navigate to Delivery Location  | Travel to the delivery point.                                                      | AND      | Delivery Location         | 1                |
| AT7     | Transport Resources            | Carry resources to the delivery location.                                         | AND      | Delivery Location         | 1                |
| AT8     | Return to Checkpoint           | Bring resources back to checkpoint if battery is low.                          | AND      | Checkpoint                | 1                |
| AT9     | Send Alert                     | Notify sector manager of failed resource return.                                 | AND      | Sector Manager's Office   | 1                |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3** (AND): Both collection and delivery are necessary for mission success.
- **G2 -> G4, G5, G6, G7** (AND): Sequential execution for collecting resources.
- **G3 -> G8, G9, G10, G11** (AND): Sequential execution for delivering resources.
- **G7 -> AT4, AT5** (AND): Sequential fallback for low battery during collection.
- **G10 -> AT8, AT9** (AND): Sequential fallback for low battery during delivery.

This model ensures efficient resource management, handles exceptions, and leverages multiple robots for parallel tasks, enhancing mission completion efficiency.
